{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785702263,"nonce":"LfIX0vXSxO2L6wdVfkAVsP2VqcM=","title":"Decided 2026-08-03 (grill; ADR-0066). The engine backstop is anchored at Attempt **claim** time (`crates/scarab-engine/src/scheduler.rs:1645-1652`), before dispatch and before the Pod exists — so **queueing delay already bills the step's timeout today**. On a busy cluster a step that waits ten minutes for a slot starts with ten minutes less than its author asked for, and if it then overruns the operator sees `Timeout` with no hint that waiting caused it. This is a live bug independent of the Depot work; the HA retry windows would only make it more visible.","message":"**Principle: waiting for infrastructure must not bill the step's execution budget.**\n\nDesign (verified cheap — the anchor is observable without an executor API change, because the executor already tracks the step container specifically in order to detect its termination for the drain):\n\n- [ ] New nullable `attempts.execution_started_at`, stamped by the scheduler the first time `poll` reports the step container running and the column is still NULL\n- [ ] The engine backstop re-anchors to `execution_started_at`, so `timeout:` measures execution — which is what authors already believe it does\n- [ ] A new **provisioning deadline** (generous default; covers scheduling, image pull and the feed), enforced as \"`execution_started_at IS NULL` and now \u003e `started_at + provisioning_deadline`\", failing with its own legible class rather than `Timeout`\n- [ ] kubelet's `activeDeadlineSeconds` becomes `provisioning_deadline + timeout` — the outer backstop, since a pod-level deadline cannot be split\n- [ ] The run budget is deliberately left alone (`enforce_run_budget` sums run-level Running intervals); note the decision rather than changing it\n- [ ] A test that a step which never starts fails as a provisioning failure naming the cause, NOT as `Timeout`\n\nFixes three things together: the Depot-outage case, the queueing case, and the \"failed as Timeout having never run\" misclassification.","files":null}]}